-$$|Y_n(\lambda)-Y(\lambda)|\le |Y_n(a)-Y(a)|+(b-a)\|G_n-G\|_\infty+L\int_a^\lambda|Y_n(r)-Y(r)|\,dr.$$
-The first two terms form a constant $A_n\to0$. Apply [F5] to $u(\lambda)=|Y_n(\lambda)-Y(\lambda)|$ to get $\sup_I|Y_n-Y|\le A_n\exp(L(b-a))\to0$. Since $\dot x_n=v_n$, this is exactly $C^1$ convergence of the coordinate curves. [step 2.1, F4, F5, algebra]
